    <paragraph>Recognize the Identity Properties of Addition and Multiplication</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, identify whether each example is using the identity property of addition or multiplication.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="158" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{3}{5}{(1)} = \frac{3}{5}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="159" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$-9 \cdot 1 = -9$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>identity property of multiplication</paragraph>
