    <heading level="1">Everyday Math</heading>
    <exercise number="210" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Insurance copayment Carrie had to have $$\text{\$80} .$$ fillings done. Each filling cost $$20\%$$ Her dental insurance required her to pay $$5$$ of the cost. Calculate Carrie’s cost</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ by finding her copay for each filling, then finding her total cost for $$5{(0.20)}{(80)}.$$ fillings, and</item>
          <item>ⓑ by multiplying $$\text{24-pound}$$</item>
          <item>ⓒ Which of the Properties of Real Numbers did you use for part (b)?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="211" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Cooking time Helen bought a $$20$$ turkey for her family’s Thanksgiving dinner and wants to know what time to put the turkey in the oven. She wants to allow $$24 \cdot 20$$ minutes per pound cooking time.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ Calculate the length of time needed to roast the turkey by multiplying $$\frac{1}{60}$$ to find the number of minutes and then multiplying the product by $$24\left( {20 \cdot \frac{1}{60}} \right).$$ to convert minutes into hours.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Multiply $$24\left( {20 \cdot \frac{1}{60}} \right)$$</item>
          <item>ⓒ Which of the Properties of Real Numbers allows you to multiply $${({24 \cdot 20})}\frac{1}{60}?$$ instead of $$(24\cdot 20)160?(24\cdot 20)160?$$</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ 8 hours</item>
          <item>ⓑ 8</item>
          <item>ⓒ associative property of multiplication</item>
        </list>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
